  "summary": "The direct transformer evidence is the four self-attention-encoder studies applied to predicting road traffic flow: [V0221] reports MetroFlow accuracy 0.84, [V0224] reports LedgerGuard F1 0.70, [V0223] reports AgriSat-4 AUROC 0.63, and [V0222] reports Atlas-ICU MAE 0.91, where MAE is an error metric so higher is worse. These values are not strictly comparable across accuracy, F1, AUROC, and MAE. No fifth supplied candidate satisfies both the transformer-method and road-traffic-topic criteria; [V0229] is included only as a forced same-topic comparator and is not transformer evidence because it uses boosted decision-tree ensembles on MetroFlow with AUROC 0.71.",
